  "status": "candidate record. Production gates were run against it locally; see verification. Owner approval for the copy change is recorded in sessionDecisions.",
  "scopeRequested": "Finish the wording change on the last surface still carrying the old label: the approved R3 homepage, whose route action, footer entry and navigation action all read \"Start here\". Copy only. No composition, geometry, asset, control or behaviour change, and no edit to any integrity-locked prototype tree.",
  "sessionDecisions": [
    "Ruling (Krish, 2026-09-24): rename every way in; on 2026-09-25 he asked for the four remaining homepage instances to be finished. There were six, three surfaces each rendered twice for the desktop and mobile variants.",
    "Changed the decision, not the markup. `decisions.sharedLanguage.selection.start` in quality/website-redesign/homepage-handoff.v1.json already drove the footer entry and the navigation action, so the homepage now says one thing in three places from one value, which is what START_LABEL does on the React side.",
    "The route stage's own action was a literal in prototypes/website-redesign-recovery/component-selection/homepage-route-configurator/index.html. That tree is integrity-locked by the handoff, so it was not edited and its hash was not rewritten to let a change pass. The prototype generator now resolves that label from the same shared-language decision, which is where it resolves every other piece of shared language.",
    "index.html under homepage-production-synthesis-r3 is generated. A first attempt hand-edited it and the prototype's own deterministic --check caught the mismatch; the edit was reverted and the generator changed instead.",
    "The original \"Start here\" wording is preserved in the handoff's provenanceNote rather than erased, alongside the owner readback it came from."
  ],
